+      <article id="journal-article" class="journal-article">
+        <p>
+          Every bag of coffee at The Daily Grind begins thousands of miles from our roastery, high in the mist-covered mountains of the Coffee Belt. Rather than purchasing anonymous commodity lots on the open exchange, our sourcing team travels each harvest season to partner directly with smallholder farms and producer cooperatives in Ethiopia, Colombia, and Guatemala. By shaking hands with the farmers who tend the trees and walking the terraced slopes alongside them, we build multi-year relationships rooted in transparency, mutual respect, and shared craftsmanship.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          Our direct-trade commitments guarantee that partnering growers receive at least 40% above Fair Trade minimum prices, with additional quality premiums awarded for micro-lots that score 87 points or higher on the Specialty Coffee Association cupping scale. Because financial stability empowers agricultural resilience, our partners can invest in shade-grown agroforestry, native canopy restoration, and organic composting rather than relying on synthetic fertilizers or high-yield monoculture hybrids that strip the soil of its character.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          During peak harvest, cherries are selectively hand-picked only when they reach a deep, uniform crimson ripeness—often requiring pickers to pass through the same orchard rows three or four times over several weeks. Within hours of picking, the fruit is delivered to local wet mills where fermentation is carefully monitored using spring water filtration and closed-loop recycling systems. Whether a lot undergoes a crisp washed process in Huila, a vibrant honey process in Antigua, or a sun-dried natural process on raised African beds in Yirgacheffe, moisture levels are tracked daily until the parchment coffee stabilizes at an ideal 11% moisture content.
+        </p>
+        <p>
+          Before any green coffee boards an ocean vessel in hermetically sealed GrainPro liners, our quality lab conducts rigorous sample roasting and blind triangulation cuppings to verify clarity, sweetness, and terroir expression. Once the sacks arrive at our local roastery, we tailor individual roast profiles for each origin—unlocking floral bergamot notes, caramelized stone fruit, and rich cocoa undertones that honor every hand that nurtured the bean from seed to cup.
+        </p>
+      </article>
+    </section>
